close_reason: Canonical metadata and implementation now agree on scoped output ownership with genuine global collision warnings.
body: "## Context\nCalendar and guide-shell both contribute to output formatting, but their registrations are bounded by command or renderer discrimination rather than competing global last-writer ownership.\n\n## Ownership rule\nCommand-bounded services and discriminated renderers are compatible scoped ownership. Unscoped registrations for the same output service remain genuine global collisions and must produce doctor warnings.\n\n## Definition of done\nA fresh sandbox with all bundled packages installed produces no false-positive output ownership warnings; an intentionally unscoped global collision still produces a doctor warning; the ownership rule is documented and regression-tested."
